# Ignore rules for this study, written root-relative so they keep working when this
# directory is published as a repository in its own right.
#
# The internal monorepo's .gitignore lives one level up and uses `*/`-prefixed patterns
# (`*/PLANNING.md`, `*/02-data/raw/**`). Those stop matching the moment this directory
# becomes the repository root, which would silently un-ignore internal planning and ~700 MB
# of raw data on the next `git add -A`. This file exists so that cannot happen.

# Internal planning — kept locally, never published.
PLANNING.md
PLAN-solo.md
HANDBOOK.md
CONTEXT.md
*.docx

# Raw and interim data never enters version control. Manifests do — provenance is the
# published artefact, the bytes are not. Every input is re-fetchable from the URL and
# hash recorded in 02-data/manifests/MANIFEST.csv.
02-data/raw/**
02-data/interim/**
!02-data/**/.gitkeep
!02-data/manifests/**

# Credentials
.env
*.key
*-service-account*.json

# Noise
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
